<unit id="f1055a1a-cc57-44e9-be2b-7ef6b0e899fa">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 2</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: # </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>WordPredictor - NVDA Add-on for Proactive Word Prediction</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="51ff7be3-8651-44d9-b25c-a2812b90233b">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 4</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>An NVDA add-on that watches what you type and predicts the next word using n-gram analysis. Predictions are announced through NVDA's own speech engine and can be accepted with keyboard shortcuts.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="eb207158-1bf0-46c7-a9bb-83fda5cdb1e8">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 6</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Why This Exists</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="363e8bca-3380-47bf-82bd-f119b823a539">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 8</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Existing word prediction tools like Lightkey Pro AT have significant accessibility barriers when used with NVDA:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="1b01e61c-e69e-4a7a-9501-4b7a46df86c1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 10</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- Gestures conflict with NVDA commands</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="aa33fb4f-3661-4d31-8ac1-0974492ae318">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 11</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- System-wide prediction requires mouse clicking</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="06bbe410-fe9f-410d-b19f-41cc8e288fcc">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 12</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- Words get mangled when pasting alongside NVDA</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="36598338-4b4a-4fff-b877-a52ef6858e51">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 14</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on solves those problems by working inside NVDA itself. No external TTS, no clipboard pasting, no mouse required. Predictions are spoken through NVDA's speech engine and inserted directly through NVDA's keyboard input system.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="5ca5f4e1-ab01-47e0-b97b-d28dc6f5d7b8">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 16</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Features</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="fc3ded70-5ce6-452b-a3cb-c963c116456d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 18</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Proactive prediction:** After you complete a word (press space or punctuation), NVDA announces up to 5 predicted next words.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f8ca0873-b216-49c6-bcba-63521034a8f8">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 19</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Partial-word prediction:** Type part of a word and press NVDA+Alt+O to get suggestions that complete what you're typing.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2d8800eb-a8a3-406d-9aa5-5b61fd75ac66">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 20</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Audible alert:** A short beep plays before predictions are announced (configurable).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="46dce2c4-4f7c-4d12-b441-f4f28fe3867a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 21</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Keyboard selection:** Press 1-5 to accept a prediction. The word is typed automatically.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="86e728e3-4309-49fa-a05a-3fdd303ff666">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 22</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Learns from your writing:** The n-gram model updates in real time as you type, learning your vocabulary and word patterns.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f84f608f-36f2-41aa-86f3-91668b091486">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 23</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Persistent learning:** Learned data saves to your NVDA user config and accumulates across restarts.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="60357917-442c-44d2-86eb-bf5bbb1ae8f1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 24</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Pre-trained:** Ships with n-gram data trained on published writing and common English word pairs, including contractions.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="daadd8d7-18d7-4939-84c7-eec0a0869024">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 25</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Toggle on/off:** Press NVDA+Alt+P to toggle prediction on or off.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e57eaae7-e098-475a-ab30-c05169909e28">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 26</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Settings panel:** Configure predictions count, beep, and learning from NVDA's Settings dialog.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4b8f95e3-9e6f-4f5e-8720-fd744e47098e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 27</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Remappable keys:** All shortcuts appear under "Word Predictor" in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="cb11cc05-18de-45cb-82ea-36fd042facd0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 28</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Works everywhere:** As a global plugin, prediction works in any application where you type text.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8c846747-2928-4243-b9ee-357f9716e32b">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 29</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Terminal-aware:** Automatically disables prediction in terminal applications (Windows Terminal, PowerShell, CMD, WSL, PuTTY, and 25+ others). Can be turned off in settings.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="766602d0-0f89-478a-aaea-489ef59acb9f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 30</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Custom app exclusion:** Add your own apps where you don't want predictions (MUD clients, code editors, chat apps with slash commands, etc.) in Settings &gt; Word Predictor. One app name per line.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="45abd738-2c98-4728-97c6-ddb4592870b0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 31</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Punctuation-aware insertion:** When you accept a prediction after a period, question mark, or exclamation point, it automatically inserts a leading space and capitalizes the first letter. After a comma, semicolon, or colon, it inserts a leading space without capitalization.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ca1f931a-7aa6-4e14-9166-68e9f77ba6de">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 33</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Key Bindings</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="bbc4faf4-96df-4c6a-8e7a-e650aff91fae">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 35</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: |</note>
<note appliesTo="source">suffix: |</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source> Key | Action </source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2130a4ef-94bc-4f9e-ba77-5b0b673267e1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 37</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: |</note>
<note appliesTo="source">suffix: |</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source> NVDA+Control+1 through NVDA+Control+0 | Accept prediction 1-10 (only intercepts when predictions are active) </source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="17d0ed3c-c53d-4c8f-b1ff-43c448510ffc">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 38</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: |</note>
<note appliesTo="source">suffix: |</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source> NVDA+Alt+P | Toggle word prediction on/off </source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="98a619a6-6206-4541-ae41-27f3d368f8ad">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 39</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: |</note>
<note appliesTo="source">suffix: |</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source> NVDA+Alt+O | Request predictions on demand (partial or full) </source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a73aef0e-07b6-4e78-bd84-dae46a5c6084">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 40</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: |</note>
<note appliesTo="source">suffix: |</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source> NVDA+Alt+L | Save learning to disk manually </source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="251c573c-7513-4aaa-ac2b-3fdcfd7796a0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 42</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>All key bindings can be remapped in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog under the "Word Predictor" category.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="770f29d1-9397-4ad5-8a34-8bc9b880ae96">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 44</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Installation</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7661b262-0eb3-4a13-b8fb-99abd278c41d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 46</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 1. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Download the latest release `.nvda-addon` file from the [releases page](https://github.com/RareBird15/wordpredictor/releases).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="5fa9c497-7590-4400-ba91-242cf96b3e7d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 47</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 2. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Open the file from Windows File Explorer to install it through NVDA's add-on installer.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d8fe0d4f-dce7-4eb6-b297-ab49c9bcd56a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 48</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 3. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Restart NVDA.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a1a0fcaf-8db3-4e2a-9fe0-be17bab0e3ba">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 50</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Usage</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="b7ac85d6-f339-48e3-bebf-5d852d4a9e9f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 52</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 1. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Start typing in any text field.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="5e1b0c21-ced7-4d8c-8f57-b5d57a9ea292">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 53</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 2. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>When you press space after a word, you'll hear a short beep followed by up to 5 predictions.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ca6f1f57-d533-4223-940b-cba56fab1557">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 54</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 3. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Press NVDA+Control+1 to accept the first prediction, NVDA+Control+2 for the second, etc.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a25f77d2-cf6d-4364-8ba5-9b9b1910e62e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 55</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 4. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The predicted word is typed automatically with a trailing space.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a3bac3ea-484e-413f-9a23-8a166ed681aa">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 56</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 5. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>For partial-word prediction, type part of a word and press NVDA+Alt+O.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="b00d4d06-9de4-41e2-b6e1-219b70650ba4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 57</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 6. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Press NVDA+Alt+P to toggle prediction on or off.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e8eacccd-8c31-4cca-8369-591a680133db">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 58</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: 7. </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Configure settings in NVDA Menu &gt; Settings &gt; Word Predictor.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0c3bd8f1-03d3-4aeb-832c-9bc290b07868">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 60</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>How It Works</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="fd8868f3-4eee-423c-b53c-9ade1ce3eab7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 62</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The add-on uses n-gram language modeling with Kneser-Ney smoothing:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="076fda4c-5257-45f8-be4c-232d84e67824">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 64</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Bigrams:** Tracks which words commonly follow other words (e.g., "the" -&gt; "system")</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e7562e38-113c-43cd-89a6-b4393dce03d7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 65</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Trigrams:** Tracks which words commonly follow two-word combinations (e.g., "I am" -&gt; "not")</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e868da59-b171-4a77-a189-2f249947526b">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 66</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Kneser-Ney smoothing:** Instead of ranking predictions by raw frequency, uses interpolated Kneser-Ney probability. This rewards words that appear in many different contexts (like "the", "is", "and") over words that appear frequently but only in specific phrases (like "York" after "New"). Handles unseen n-grams gracefully by backing off to lower-order n-grams with adjusted probabilities.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="53e3274c-e701-4737-af7b-b8bd92a5cbaf">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 67</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Three-level interpolation:** Trigram probability is blended with bigram probability, which is blended with unigram continuation probability. This means even words never seen in the exact context still get a probability based on how common they are as continuations.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="cccdb7e9-3f98-40a5-a08d-4895da90e5c4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 68</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Partial matching:** When you type part of a word, the add-on searches all n-grams for words that start with what you've typed and ranks them by KN probability</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c47b439b-5df6-4414-954f-bfe28005a0bc">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 69</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Real-time learning:** Every word you type updates the n-gram counts and derived statistics, so the model adapts to your writing style</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2b97538a-b63c-4869-985e-6cfe2d2a8f47">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 70</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Persistent storage:** Learning saves to `wordPredictor_learned.json` in your NVDA user config directory</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="87482fd9-c89b-40a4-b4e7-7871dc57fd78">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 71</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **Backward compatible:** Existing learned data from v1.1.0 loads without migration. Smoothing can be turned off in settings to restore the original frequency-based behavior.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="65ff22b3-e853-4046-bf7f-c08a8986e6c1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 73</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The n-gram data is stored as a JSON file and loaded at startup. No external Python dependencies are required.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7f0225ae-3cb3-403d-afe7-3427fa1529bb">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 75</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Technical Details</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d697a7e8-fff4-4dac-8094-c4d7cddc7cac">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 77</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- **NVDA version:** Requires NVDA 2026.1 or later (Python 3.13, 64-bit)</source>
</segment>
